                        ],
                        "form": "наше́дшийся"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "10904383-ac14-481c-aa59-f7812d39e191",
                        "entry_id": "25abe57e-35f5-398f-a5ad-101da72c9e04",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "найдя́сь"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90c05887-91b2-3043-ae39-565433bcb676",
                        "entry_id": "25abe57e-35f5-398f-a5ad-101da72c9e04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "обнаружиться, отыскаться"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b4b9559-a3f6-4e9e-b624-d1b2efd2a5c6",
                                "sense_id": "90c05887-91b2-3043-ae39-565433bcb676",
                                "text": "Мама Язгуль очень плакала, когда узнала, что нашлась родная мать."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c99e0ec6-2384-42a0-93eb-d942b03598fc",
                                "sense_id": "90c05887-91b2-3043-ae39-565433bcb676",
                                "text": "Записная книдка нашлась в кармане пальто."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "446cbec6-e208-4a56-b6e6-b31a5985a144",
                                "sense_id": "90c05887-91b2-3043-ae39-565433bcb676",
                                "text": "У вас спичек не найдётся?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "afe758de-27be-3071-b967-0138b57c5f8c",
                        "entry_id": "25abe57e-35f5-398f-a5ad-101da72c9e04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "оказаться в наличии"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c110b34-2531-4daa-8b92-4ee509ad2e9f",
                                "sense_id": "afe758de-27be-3071-b967-0138b57c5f8c",
                                "text": "Впрочем, были бы деньги — программы найдутся."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9ad9e2f7-914e-3514-adc4-cfdc7b10bd8d",
                        "entry_id": "25abe57e-35f5-398f-a5ad-101da72c9e04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг., неодобр. выражает неудовольствие по поводу какого-либо субъекта и сомнение в наличии у него необходимых положительных качеств"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "3-е лицо, прош. вр."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bd820ce-d202-486c-a54e-7a7f5beccf2c",
                                "sense_id": "9ad9e2f7-914e-3514-adc4-cfdc7b10bd8d",
                                "text": "— Тоже мне искусствовед нашёлся!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2850e861-d4d4-3ac0-af85-48d113b6a713",
                        "entry_id": "25abe57e-35f5-398f-a5ad-101da72c9e04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. не растеряться, правильно повести себя в сложной ситуации"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c89864be-69e0-4933-913f-c430d655542f",
                                "sense_id": "2850e861-d4d4-3ac0-af85-48d113b6a713",
                                "text": "Я слегка окаменел и не нашёлся что ответить."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e06102a-87ab-4cce-a88f-d1b40571d44f",
                        "source_entry_id": "25abe57e-35f5-398f-a5ad-101da72c9e04",
                        "source_sense_description": "оказаться в наличии",
                        "target_lang_word": "appear",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "appear",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d336e655-5dfa-3642-bea6-4319867488da",
                                        "entry_id": "891200c3-7bb7-350c-91f9-b00b5b27e0fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To come or be in sight; to be in view; to become visible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55075a1c-5703-4635-acca-0992d49a8b04",
                                                "sense_id": "d336e655-5dfa-3642-bea6-4319867488da",
                                                "text": "And God[…]said, Let[…]the dry land appear."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ac9e514-efae-4b53-b208-d8080031cf80",
                                                "sense_id": "d336e655-5dfa-3642-bea6-4319867488da",
                                                "text": "There were also particles no one had predicted that just appeared. Five of them […, i]n order of increasing modernity, […] are the neutrino, the pi meson, the antiproton, the quark and the Higgs boson."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a67bfda-99f4-3221-9966-64362fc58973",
                                        "entry_id": "891200c3-7bb7-350c-91f9-b00b5b27e0fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To come before the public."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b67eb785-6a19-41a9-a16a-b19367668f5e",
                                                "sense_id": "4a67bfda-99f4-3221-9966-64362fc58973",
                                                "text": "A great writer appeared at that time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9da74b70-f034-4c23-86a0-bd33d46d36d8",
                                                "sense_id": "4a67bfda-99f4-3221-9966-64362fc58973",
                                                "text": "Miss Phyllis Morgan, as the hapless heroine dressed in the shabbiest of clothes, appears in the midst of a gay and giddy throng; she apostrophises all and sundry there, including the villain, and has a magnificent scene which always brings down the house, and nightly adds to her histrionic laurels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5dee07b-9d1f-3e4f-a373-2239b6fdd245",
                                        "entry_id": "891200c3-7bb7-350c-91f9-b00b5b27e0fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To stand in presence of some authority, tribunal, or superior person, to answer a charge, plead a cause, etc.; to present oneself as a party or advocate before a court, or as a person to be tried."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a395add8-91b7-475d-a5f8-e7ec5b2d0215",
                                                "sense_id": "c5dee07b-9d1f-3e4f-a373-2239b6fdd245",
                                                "text": "We must all appear before the judgment seat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccd182f3-ccbb-4f63-89d4-b75ab12becb3",
                                                "sense_id": "c5dee07b-9d1f-3e4f-a373-2239b6fdd245",
                                                "text": "One ruffian escaped because no prosecutor dared to appear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c869e398-13ad-3aac-8231-e066afd76fe0",
                                        "entry_id": "891200c3-7bb7-350c-91f9-b00b5b27e0fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become visible to the apprehension of the mind; to be known as a subject of observation or comprehension, or as a thing proved; to be obvious or manifest."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "541adcdf-063f-420e-9c89-aa5816a253f7",
                                                "sense_id": "c869e398-13ad-3aac-8231-e066afd76fe0",
                                                "text": "It doth not yet appear what we shall be."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "066f90a4-962e-4e74-a89c-5477ea82cc9f",
                                                "sense_id": "c869e398-13ad-3aac-8231-e066afd76fe0",
                                                "text": "Of their vain contest appeared no end."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff72273a-ec5f-4e1a-949d-26cf6b4ac20f",
                                                "sense_id": "c869e398-13ad-3aac-8231-e066afd76fe0",
                                                "text": "‘Then the father has a great fight with his terrible conscience,’ said Munday with granite seriousness. ‘Should he make a row with the police[…]? Or should he say nothing about it and condone brutality for fear of appearing in the newspapers?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b584c95-487e-4824-83f2-4af99458a3a0",
                                                "sense_id": "c869e398-13ad-3aac-8231-e066afd76fe0",
                                                "text": "Surprisingly, this analysis revealed that acute exposure to solvent vapors at concentrations below those associated with long-term effects appears to increase the risk of a fatal automobile accident. Furthermore, this increase in risk is comparable to the risk of death from leukemia after long-term exposure to benzene,[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bbe3e3b5-6e75-35d1-8c5a-f97b8fa6367e",
                                        "entry_id": "891200c3-7bb7-350c-91f9-b00b5b27e0fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To seem; to have a certain semblance; to look."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "copulative",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41cb82a5-f1cd-441d-9169-9612dbb05a7e",
                                                "sense_id": "bbe3e3b5-6e75-35d1-8c5a-f97b8fa6367e",
                                                "text": "He appeared quite happy with the result."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5763d019-23e2-4bd3-a319-87c686bb18d3",
                                                "sense_id": "bbe3e3b5-6e75-35d1-8c5a-f97b8fa6367e",
                                                "text": "They disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58e77aa8-8a36-4c36-a532-9b318b7b87f6",
                                                "sense_id": "bbe3e3b5-6e75-35d1-8c5a-f97b8fa6367e",
                                                "text": "Mr. Campion appeared suitably impressed and she warmed to him. He was very easy to talk to with those long clown lines in his pale face, a natural goon, born rather too early she suspected."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb736d3e-77b0-30d0-9499-71be1963f286",
                                        "entry_id": "891200c3-7bb7-350c-91f9-b00b5b27e0fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bring into view."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "695172af-a540-4e96-a558-de8a57b0f42d",
                                                "sense_id": "bb736d3e-77b0-30d0-9499-71be1963f286",
                                                "text": "[Angelo] is yet a devil / His filth within being cast, he would appear / A pond as deep as hell."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
